		Anekdots: {
			Anekdot0:
				'''
				Teacher: I killed a person. Tom Green, convert this sentence into Future Tense, please.
				Student Tom Green: You will go to jail.
				'''
			Anekdot1:
				'''
				What does my dad have in common with Nemo?
				They both can’t be found.
				'''
			Anekdot2:
				'''
				When does a joke become a dad joke?
				When it leaves and never comes back.
				'''
			Anekdot3:
				'''
				Patient: “Where exactly are you taking me, doctor?”
				Doctor: “To the morgue.”
				Patient: “What? But I’m not dead yet!”
				Doctor: “And we’re not there yet.”
				'''
			Anekdot4:
				'''
				You don’t need a parachute to go skydiving.
				You need a parachute to go skydiving twice.
				'''
			Anekdot5:
				'''
				Son: How do stars die?
				Dad: An overdose, usually.
				'''
			Anekdot6:
				'''
				Two hunters are in the woods when one of them collapses.
				His hunting buddy immediately calls 911. “My friend isn’t breathing,”
				He shouts into the phone. “What should I do?”
				“Relax,” the operator tells him. “I can help. First, let’s make sure he’s dead.”
				There’s silence and then a gunshot.
				The guy gets back on the phone and says, “OK, now what?”
				'''
			Anekdot7:
				'''
				My wife and I have made a difficult choice and have decided we do not want children.
				If anybody does, please just send me your contact details,
				And we can drop them off tomorrow.
				'''
			Anekdot8:
				'''
				Doctor: “I have good and bad news.”
				Patient: “Give me the good news first.”
				Doctor: “Your test results are back, and you have only two days to live.”
				Patient: “That’s the good news? What’s the bad news?”
				Doctor: “I’ve been trying to reach you for two days.”
				'''
			Anekdot9:
				'''
				Son: Dad, if I told you I was gay, would you still love me?
				Dad: Don’t be silly son, you were an accident. I never loved you in the first place.
				'''
			Anekdot10:
				'''
				Wife: I’m pregnant.
				Husband: Hi pregnant, I’m dad.
				Wife: No, you’re not.
				'''
			Anekdot11:
				'''
				Every time my grandmother and I were at a wedding she’d say:
				“you’re next”. So I started saying the same thing to her at funerals.
				'''
			Anekdot12: Jokes about ISIS are all about the execution.
			Anekdot13: "If you think I would joke about Alzheimer’s, forget it. "
		}
	}

